Revision history for PDL-EEG

0.05  (unreleased)
  CHANGED
    - PDL::EEG::TFA: faster convolution engine, same coefficients (agreement
      with the previous implementation to rounding, <= 2e-13 relative).
      The signal FFT is computed once and reused for every frequency; all
      trials of tfr_morlet / tfr_superlet / tfr_stat are transformed
      together in blocks; the FFT length is a product of 2, 3 and 5 just
      above ntime + the longest kernel half-length (was the next power of
      two above ntime + kernel length, per frequency); tfr_morlet only
      accumulates what the requested output needs. Measured on Linux,
      PDL 2.085: cwt_morlet on 297000 samples x 14 frequencies 3.4 s ->
      0.9 s; tfr_morlet (output => 'all') on 292 x 2500 samples x 14
      frequencies 4.5 s -> 1.1 s; tfr_morlet power on 400 x 1701 samples x
      167 frequencies 49 s -> 8 s. t/16_tfa.t: comparison with a direct
      time-domain convolution, trials together vs one at a time, block
      size independence.
  ADDED
    - PDL::EEG::GED: generic GED spatial filter (ged_cov / ged_operator /
      apply_ged; S w = lambda R w via PDL::LinearAlgebra sygvd, R-orthonormal
      filters, biorthogonal patterns A = R W, shrinkage regularisation on R)
      and a vEOG-guided blink workflow (detect_blinks / blink_free /
      blink_evoked / fit_blink / remove_blinks). Single blink component only.
    - PDL::EEG::Regress: regress_out() -- temporal nuisance / EOG regression.
    - PDL::EEG::Heartbeat: detect_r, beat_epochs, beat_average, surrogate_r,
      bn_balance.
    - PDL::EEG::Heartbeat::Respiration: respiratory phase from beat-to-beat
      series of the heartbeat (rr_series, r_amplitude, resp_phase, phase_at,
      phase_locking). t/25_respiration.t (synthetic recording with a known
      breathing phase).
    - PDL::EEG::Filter: filters along the time axis. zp_butter (zero-phase
      Butterworth in the frequency domain; it was in PDL::EEG::Heartbeat, which
      no longer exports it), analytic_signal, envelope, inst_phase.
      t/24_filter.t (reference values from scipy filtfilt and hilbert).
    - PDL::EEG::MAP2D: plot_joint (all channels coloured by electrode position,
      scalp maps at chosen latencies tied to the waveforms); examples/
      heartbeat_joint.pl; t/23_joint.t.
    - PDL::EEG::MAP2D plot_topomap: when drawn into the caller's axes
      (_ax / _fig), colorbar => { ... } attaches a colour bar of
      PDL::Graphics::Cairo to that axes (t/15).
    - PDL::EEG::MAP2D: grid_layout_1020 -- the 19 electrodes of the 10-20
      system as a 5x5 grid of panels (row and column per channel name, old and
      new names, and the free cell for a scalp map). (t/15)
    - examples/avg_grid_scrub.pl: a tab-separated average as a 5x5 grid of
      panels laid out like the 10-20 system, with a scalp map that follows the
      latency chosen by click or drag (show_grid_scrub of PDL::Graphics::Cairo).
    - examples/heartbeat_hep_scalp.pl: R-locked scalp maps in the recorded
      reference against non-heartbeat time points, BN1/BN2 two-lead fits.
    - examples/heartbeat_bne_survey.pl, t/22_heartbeat.t (deterministic
      synthetic ECG; R-peak reference values from an independent
      implementation).
    - PDL::EEG::Spans: time-interval span annotations, .spans.tsv sidecar,
      spans_to_mask / kinds_present.
    - PDL::EEG::ICA: pure-PDL symmetric FastICA (whiten / fastica /
      ica_decompose / identify_by_reference / apply_ica / ica_operator).
    - examples: blink_ged_clean.pl (GED blink removal, .edf/.mul output),
      artifact_remove.pl (multi-class GED / regression removal with per-artifact
      reference covariance, review image, --rank diagnostic), raw_plot.pl
      (interactive span annotator), task_ica_mul.pl (ICA blink + horizontal
      removal -> .mul), ged_vs_ica_blink.pl (GED-vs-ICA comparison).
    - t/18_ged.t, t/19_regress.t, t/20_spans.t, t/21_ica.t (synthetic,
      render-free).
    - PDL::EEG::TFA POD: FUNCTIONS section documenting all six exported
      functions (morlet_wavelet, cwt_morlet, tfr_morlet, tfr_superlet,
      tfr_stat, apply_baseline) from the implementation and t/16_tfa.t.
  FIXED
    - NihonKohden wfmblock: channel-table off-by-one (electrode code was read
      from the first byte of the next record). Contiguous 10-20 codes were
      unaffected; every aux channel was shifted by one. Labels only, data
      untouched. extblock path unchanged.
    - EDF write_edf: an EDF+ recording-identification field already starting
      with "Startdate" (as read_edf returns it) is passed through verbatim
      instead of being re-wrapped, which had produced a double-"Startdate"
      header rejected by EDFBrowser.
    - per-module $VERSION removed from GED, ICA, Regress, Spans (added after
      0.04 with their own version strings; the single source is lib/PDL/EEG.pm).
    - t/15_map2d.t: read the tracked fixture t/data/standard_1020_subset.elc,
      so the test runs on a clean clone instead of being skipped.
  DOCS
    - t/data/NOTICE: provenance and license (GPL-3.0-or-later) of the two .elc
      fixtures (FieldTrip, New York Head).
    - README.md: 85 lines that had been double-encoded in 0.04 (UTF-8 bytes
      re-read as Latin-1 and re-encoded, so "—" rendered as "â" plus control
      characters) restored to the pre-0.04 text; no other line touched.
    - Nihon Kohden docs consolidated under doc/ (docs/ retired):
      NihonKohden.md overview, NK_block_layouts.md/.ja.md, NK_extblock.md,
      NK_files.md.
    - README: new modules, examples, artifact-removal workflow, tests.

0.04  2026-09-02
    - version consolidated to a single source (lib/PDL/EEG.pm); per-module $VERSION removed
    - MAP2D::plot_topomap: head_extent option (grow the head circle toward the
      axes edges; with PDL::Graphics::Cairo 0.2+ an axis('off') topomap panel can
      carry its own colour bar)
    - examples/sep_gof_sweep.pl: best-single-dipole goodness-of-fit swept over
      latency (ms<TAB>gof), for the movie's --gof
    - examples/sep_nonHFO_movie.3panel.pl: three-panel SEP latency movie
      (waveforms | 2D topomap | ECD GoF), equal-width columns, polarity-coloured traces

0.035   (unreleased)
  ADDED
    - PDL::EEG::IO::ASA: read ASA electrode-position files (.elc), the library
      form of the PDL Advent Calendar 2024 (Day 12) parser. read_elc() returns
      a (3,N) coordinate piddle, parallel labels, a name->xyz lookup, unit /
      reference metadata, and detected fiducials (LPA/RPA/Nz). Robust to
      indented coordinate blocks and CRLF; the coordinate block is parsed
      vectorised (flat list -> reshape) rather than row-by-row. The declared
      NumberPositions= is cross-checked and a mismatch is carped.
    - parse_ELEC_POS3D_ASA_4AdventCalendar(): drop-in shim reproducing the
      Advent parser's four-value return, so existing scripts keep working.
    - examples/show_electrodes_3d.pl: 3D scalp-electrode viewer over read_elc,
      with GS3D (PDL::Graphics::Cairo::Driver::GS3D) and TriD backends; both
      renderers are optional (loaded on demand, not added to prereqs).
    - t/14_asa.t and t/data/standard_1020_subset.elc: 28-point real-coordinate
      fixture (19ch + Fpz/Oz + M1/M2 + A1/A2 + LPA/RPA/Nz).

0.03   2026-07-18
  BREAKING
    - .LOG events now carry data-sample positions ({samp}/{t_data}). extblock
      placement corrected: the .LOG elapsed-seconds clock also counts paused
      time between recording blocks, so anchoring events to it drifted them by
      tens to hundreds of seconds and misfiled late segments (some clamped to
      the data end). Events are now placed by REC START-delimited segments
      against exact block boundaries; task-marker positions in multi-segment
      files change (and are now correct). Re-epoch any saved event positions.
  ADDED
    - clock_to_samp() maps wall-clock to samples through block_meta (piecewise,
      break-aware); nk_to_mul.pl --cut-clock is now correct across recording
      breaks (was a naive wall==data map that leaked the next block into a cut).
    - wfmblock: .LOG events are placed for concatenated multi-block reads
      (all_blocks); previously wfmblock events had no sample position at all.
    - xt/70_real_data.t: real-data event-placement regression (extblock +
      wfmblock; REC STARTs land exactly on block boundaries).
  FIXED
    - lib/PDL/EEG.pm: malformed $VERSION line (the module did not compile;
      `use PDL::EEG` died). Also refreshed the module list (EDF is implemented).

0.02   2026-07-17
  BREAKING
    - extblock multi-segment read; DC returned in µV (was 1000x low);
      gap_samples default 0; DC numbering by format signature (unknown croaks).
  ADDED
    - mul_to_nk.pl --solve-bne; {units}/{n_samp_per_block}/{block_meta};
      read_mul; per-signal EDF dimension; t/13; mk_synthetic_nk --long.

0.01  2026-06-12
    - Initial release
    - PDL::EEG::IO::NihonKohden: read Nihon Kohden EEG-1100C binary files
      - Confirmed format from real hardware (EEG-1100C, JE-921A amplifier)
      - Waveform data: uint16 offset binary, 0.09765625 µV/bit
      - Sampling rate auto-detected from wfmblock header (+0x1A lower 14 bits)
      - Channel labels from .21E file (CRLF-aware) with DEFAULT_LABELS fallback
      - BCD timestamp decode (YY/MM/DD HH:MM:SS)
      - Event parsing from .LOG file (ASCII 6-digit seconds format)
      - n_samples computed from inter-block gap
      - Multi-block support (block => N option)
    - examples/verify_read.pl: step-by-step verification tool
    - examples/read_nihonkohden.pl: interactive viewer with giza_server sliders
      - Horizontal slider: time axis scroll
      - Vertical slider: gain (µV/div)
      - Decimation for render performance (step_max=5)
